{"id": "EUVD-2026-104290", "enisaUuid": "370e6d60-5f27-3ebf-8430-fd228f89da4b", "description": "VideoLAN libbluray through 1.5.1 contains an uncontrolled memory allocation vulnerability in _parse_extent_start_points() in clpi_parse.c that trusts the num_point field without bounds checking. Attackers can supply a crafted .clpi file on a disc, image, or directory with a huge num_point to exhaust memory and CPU, causing denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T02:53:35", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libbluray-clpi-ep-map-oob-read", "https://code.videolan.org/videolan/libbluray/-/blob/1.5.1/src/libbluray/bdnav/clpi_parse.c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libbluray-through-1.5.1-uncontrolled-memory-allocation-via-parse-extent-start-points"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112283", "GHSA-2xfh-28f7-pm5w"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ffaa7c27-a8cf-3408-849a-0e9141ec0ddb", "product": {"name": "libbluray", "vendor": {"name": "libbluray"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.5.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6b4d57c6-0de9-3bd6-856d-02fe80615574", "vendor": {"name": "VideoLAN"}}], "isExploited": false}